<title>USA: Polaroid Corp may issue $250 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Polaroid Corp may issue $250 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polaroid Corp is expected to issue a $250 million debt offering on Monday or Tuesday, high-grade syndicate sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is talk of Polaroid bringing a $250 million debt issue consisting of an intermediate maturity,&quot; one syndicate source said.</p>
<p>The Polaroid issue is expected to be underwritten by lead manager Lehman Brothers, and is rated Baa3 by Moody's Investors Service Inc and BBB by Standard &amp; Poors.</p>
<p>No further details were immediately available on the deal.</p>
<p>((--Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675))</p>
